Title: F1-M06 — The Broken Dam (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. VALLEY GARRISON RADIO ROOM - MORNING

[[AMBIENCE: water roaring through the window, a bell ringing somewhere, a handset crackling]]
[[MUSIC: urgent, rising]]

A soaked map of the valley is weighted down with a wrench. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it. ENGINEER VENN's voice comes through the handset.

ENGINEER VENN (V.O.)
(breathless, over radio)
The dam is failing. We have minutes before the lower road becomes a river.

MIRA
(serious)
The enemy is still on the eastern bank. Our engineers and the local workers are trapped between them and the water.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: control house below the dam to the north, stone bridge and village to the north-east, low road down the valley floor, pumping yard, ridge high ground to the south]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
Evacuate the workers, recover the engineers, and get every surviving unit to the marked high ground before the timer expires.

ENGINEER VENN (V.O.)
(urgent, over radio)
Riflemen on the service road between us and you. On foot we do not get past them. Whatever comes for us, send it with guns.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Two amphibious craft and one light transport. The village first; the water reaches it before it reaches you.

MIRA
(dry)
Seventeen minutes on Venn's estimate. I would plan for less. Anything on tracks still north of the dip when the road goes under stays there.

ENGINEER VENN (V.O.)
(focused, over radio)
Captain, the crest is going at one point only. A dam does not break neatly by itself.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
Tell me on the ridge, Venn. Move.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
